    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0338" n="248" xml:id="pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123So.8/62: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul at Aden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Southard</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-03T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1920—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s June 11th, 6 p.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d198-f1"/> Vice
                    Consul Town-send has been ordered proceed Aden from Saloniki to take charge
                    office temporarily. Upon his arrival you may proceed Abyssinia for visit. You
                    should not proceed with the Anglo-American Oil party or do anything which would
                    give them any appearance of being an official organization or having official
                    support other than that which would be naturally extended to any American doing
                    business in foreign country. However you will, of course, render them every
                    assistance practicable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
